  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">5-year programme for the prevention and elimination of FGM and Child marriage in</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">About 97% of girls in Guinea are subjected to violence in the form of female genital mutilation (FGM) and about 67% are married off early as children. Some girls die and many suffer health complications or psychological trauma. Child mothers also face high risks of obstetric fistula or maternal death during childbirth, and are denied their education. This project will work holistically in four districts sensitising communities to abandon FGM and child marriage (especially through religious leaders and school clubs), motivating excisors to abandon FGM and law enforcers to implement laws, and referring survivors for support services. It will use lessons learned for advocacy across Africa.</narrative>
  </description>
